          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: der Schimmel",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "der Schimmel — \"the mould (US: mold); a white horse\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In der Ecke vom Bad ist Schimmel. There is mould in the corner of the bathroom."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "No plural for mould. Ein Schimmel is also a white horse."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Schimmel is inherited from Middle High German schimel (EtymDB). Dutch schimmel 'mould' is a cousin; the white horse is usually said to be named for its mould-white colour."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
